 loc='\U0001f4cd Near Rolde / Grolloo \u00b7 Woodland and heath \u00b7 Medium-sized',
 desc='<b>Vijftig Bunder</b>, like De Twintig Bunders further on, carries its origin in its name: fifty bunder \u2014 about fifty hectares \u2014 was the size of the parcel cut as a single block from the common heath after the <b>Marken Act of 1886</b>. That the people of Drenthe simply named their new parcels after their acreage says something about how abrupt that division was: centuries-old field names gave way to bookkeeping labels. The block was planted with <b>Scots pine</b>, and that wood still stands, now a mature stand with heavy trunks. Along the edges and in a few clearings the <b>original heath</b> has been preserved or brought back by sod cutting. Management works towards more variety: <b>thinning, introducing broadleaf and leaving dead wood</b>. The result is a wood in which <b>black woodpecker, goshawk and pine marten</b> are at home, with viviparous lizard and grayling on the open heath.',
